	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nResistor calculations:\nPer the datasheet, we use the following equations to verify phils lab values:\n	Vout = 0.6(1 + R1/R2)\n		AND\n	R2 = (0.6V * R1)/(Vout - 0.6V)\nFor 1V output:\n	Vout = 0.6(1 + 68k/100k) = 1.008 V\nFor 1.8V output:\n	Vout = 0.6(1 + 200k/100k) = 1.8V\nFor 3V output: \n	Vout = 0.6(1 + 453k/100k) = 3.32V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 189.23 55.88 0)
		(size 35.56 31.75)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "10b6d0cb-8fe8-4e76-a51d-b898c9fbfa51")
	)
	(text_box "[${#}] ${TITLE}"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8 13.97 0)
		(size 105.41 12.7)
		(margins 4.4999 4.4999 4.4999 4.4999)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Times New Roman")
				(size 6 6)
				(thickness 1.2)
				(bold yes)
				(color 162 22 34 1)
			)
		)
		(uuid "11d05840-f080-4878-a99a-dca3b8eee82e")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nUsed 22p cap per data sheet: \n	\"In some applications, adding a 22pF ceramic\n	cap in parallel with R1 may further speed up the load\n	transient responses and is thus recommended for\n	applications with large load transient step requirements.\"\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 85.09 0)
		(size 28.194 25.4)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21ec4d16-3c7c-4e41-b1ba-1a96f91d121d")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nUsed pull up resistor per data sheet: \n	\"Connect a pull-up resistor to the input.\"\n\n100k is a common value but we can use the equation:\n	Rmin > Vpullup/1mA = 5k\n1mA is generally low enough to maintain LOW"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 154.94 0)
		(size 28.194 25.4)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2914cdc3-b16f-4b36-9d13-518b9d3e3286")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nFor each rail (5 V → 1.0/1.8/3.3 V) using L = 2.2 µH and f_SW = 1 MHz, the inductor ripple current is approximately 0.36-0.52 A. With a maximum load of 0.51-1 A, the peak inductor current stays below 1.3 A, which is well under the SRP2512A-2R2M's 3 A saturation rating and 2.27 A RMS current rating. DC losses are at most ~100 mW at 1 A (DCR ≤ 98 mΩ), so the chosen inductor comfortably meets the electrical and thermal requirements."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 153.67 16.51 0)
		(size 31.75 34.29)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "402879c6-93b7-4681-9a17-a4bae6900e9f")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nUsed cermaic capacitor cap per data sheet: \n	\"IN 3 Power input pin. Decouple this pin to GND pin with at least 10µF ceramic cap.\"\n\n22u is a common value used in the example schematic and recommended by Phil's lab\n\nWe use a Murata GRT21BR61A226ME13L (22 µF, 10 V, X5R, 0805) on each input. At 5 V bias, a typical 22 µF X5R 0805 loses roughly half its capacitance, so we assume an effective capacitance of ~11 µF. This still satisfies the ≥10 µF datasheet minimum while providing low ESR and enough charge to support the 1 MHz switching current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 158.75 0)
		(size 40.894 36.83)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7b018a3e-1a8e-4c30-85c9-fcaafd82dc02")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nFor the best performance, it is recommend d to use X5R or better grade ceramic capacitor with 6.3V rating and greater than 22µF capacitance. \n\nWe again use the 22 µF Murata GRT21 on each rail (1.0 V, 1.8 V, 3.3 V). With L = 2.2 µH and VIN = 5 V, the worst-case inductor ripple is about ΔI_L ≈ 0.52 A on the 1.8 V rail. The RMS ripple current in the output capacitor is approximated as:\n\n𝐼Crms = Δ𝐼L / 2sqrt(3) ≈ 0.15 A\n\nSo each output capacitor sees ≈0.15 A RMS ripple, which is well within the capability of a 22 µF X5R 0805 MLCC and consistent with the SY8003's own note that a single 22 µF X5R can handle the ripple current for several-amp loads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 154.94 119.38 0)
		(size 74.93 30.48)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 3 9 250 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3d56edc-7e84-4b8c-b9c2-00a700272d3d")
	)
